※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4515

※ What `⎕enumerate` makes is an iterator, and a loop is the only thing that
※ takes one: there is no type for an iterator in this language and nothing else
※ to do with one.  So it stands after the `=` of a `foreach` and nowhere else.

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    let v: u8⟦2⟧ = ⟦1u8, 2u8⟧
    let held: u8 = ⎕enumerate(v)
    0u6
